{
  "dom_id": "step-q97686",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Lucy's marbles are labeled with numbers $-3$ through $8.$ If Lucy chooses a marble at random, what is the expected value of the chosen marble?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number on the chosen marble. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{-3,-2,…,8\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{-3,-2,…,8\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-3+8}{2}=2.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen marble is $2.5.$",
